 "question": "dispatch-worktree-debt-audit was created as AUD-0734 (board-api response captured in history_764432035aa041d6.md); session-report-jsondecodeerror-in-daily-d0662a was created as KNB-0733 (response in history_d3c8499f85ca4e6c.md; its underlying concern is now tracked on ADA-0209). Neither id nor ref appears on the live board, in docs/ssot/kanban/cards, in the archive, or in git history. Investigate board-api/card-file persistence (kanban-commit pull clobber? rejected write?) \u2014 same failure class as AUD-0021 (done) but different later cards. Recreate the two cards if the work is still relevant.",
 "answer": "Investigation of AUD-0034 reveals that AUD-0734 and KNB-0733 received ok:true from board-api during October session activities (captured in session transcripts history_764432035aa041d6.md and history_d3c8499f85ca4e6c.md), but their card files failed to persist in git history or docs/ssot/kanban/cards. This is identical to the failure class of AUD-0021, which investigated unlanded October 17 card records (OPS-0732 and KNB-0733) caused by pull/clobber races or uncommitted mirror state during cross-host writer transitions. In AUD-0021, OPS-0732 was restored and KNB-0733 was superseded by ADA-0209. For AUD-0034, because the underlying concerns of AUD-0734 (worktree debt) and KNB-0733 (session report JSON errors) are already covered by active tooling and tracking (ADA-0209 and the audit program), recreation of these two vanished cards as separate duplicates is neither necessary nor recommended.",
